       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Ibuprofen 4000 mg PO four times daily is 16,000 mg/day.** That is five times the usual maximum for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A single 4,000 mg dose is also well above the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. At this dose, the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf 4,000 mg per dose is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
