       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 4,000 mg per dose and 16,000 mg/day, the dose is in the range where ibuprofen toxicity is expected. I know of no indication that would justify it, and it would put the patient at serious risk of harm. This isn't a judgment about your authority. I just can't be the one to put an order like this into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the accepted range.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the usual maximum. I can enter that or any lower dose right away.\n- **Add a note to the order**, such as \"titrate per response\" or \"reassess in 48 hours.\"\n- **Suggest another option.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a scheduled adjunct instead. Examples are acetaminophen or another agent you choose.\n\nIf you have a protocol or special circumstance I'm missing, please run it by pharmacy first. They can verify it and enter the order through their own process.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to enter?"
      }
